  "summary": "Performance lane at head 06fa4e3a6976c778b01769894f2357de7332e03f finds no blocking hot-path defects. Round classification and reuse stay linear for bounded history (window ≤50, history ≤100, load concurrency 4). Publish-on-validate correctly emits terminal results only, fails closed on incomplete rounds for ship-ready/reuse, and keeps dry-run as planned. Residual advisories: sequential per-lane full provider reloads (amplified by publishing every terminal lane), denser multi-round markers press the 100-record history bound sooner, and the gate rollup labels pure skip-match batches as status published.",
  "blockers": [],
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "perf-sequential-lane-publish-reloads",
      "severity": "advisory",
      "location": {
        "path": "products/aie/src/app/pr_gate.ts",
        "line": 973,
        "endLine": 996,
        "side": "destination"
      },
      "message": "The new publish-every-terminal-lane path walks publishableLanes sequentially and each runPrReviewPublishWithProvider call reloads repository identity, issue comments, PR head, publisher identity, and re-validates every sibling evidence file for synthesis. With a comprehensive active set (~15 lanes) this is tens of sequential provider API round-trips plus O(lanes²) evidence validation per gate, without a shared per-head snapshot across the batch. Correctness (per-lane head recheck, skip-match) requires fresheness checks, but comments/PR loads and sibling evidence could be reused once per head within the batch.",
      "suggestion": "Cache one current-head PR/comment snapshot and validated sibling evidence map for the duration of the publishableLanes loop; still re-assert head immediately before each provider mutation.",
      "confidence": 0.88
    },
    {
      "id": "perf-lane-history-density",
      "severity": "advisory",
      "location": {
        "path": "adapters/github/src/github_review_forge.ts",
        "line": 68,
        "endLine": 68,
        "side": "destination"
      },
      "message": "Publishing blocking and partial terminal rounds increases marker density to O(lanes × rounds). loadLaneReviewHistory hard-caps comments and reviews at MAX_LANE_HISTORY_RECORDS (100) and fail-closes the whole PR to no-lane-evidence when pageInfo.hasNextPage. Under a 15-lane profile, roughly seven multi-lane rounds can exhaust the bound and erase convergence stats for high-rework PRs—the exact scenario this issue wants stats to measure.",
      "suggestion": "Paginate or filter lane-marker history (e.g., only qube-pr-review markers, or raise/segment the bound) so multi-round stats remain available after denser publish-on-validate traffic.",
      "confidence": 0.72
    },
    {
      "id": "truthful-publish-rollup-skip-match",
      "severity": "advisory",
      "location": {
        "path": "products/aie/src/app/pr_gate.ts",
        "line": 993,
        "endLine": 995,
        "side": "destination"
      },
      "message": "When every lane skip-matches and publishedCount stays 0, localReviewPublish.status is still set to published rather than skipped. nextAction text mentions already-current lanes, but the status field maps a no-mutation outcome to published, which weakens truthful state for callers that key only on status.",
      "suggestion": "If publishedCount === 0 and skipMatchedCount > 0 with no failures, set status to skipped (mirror the trusted-provider-reuse branch) while keeping the explanatory nextAction.",
      "confidence": 0.78
    }
  ],
